# H2b (SOFT, quad, RUN LAST but one): the TIMED pass of H2 (watcher OFF) over the arms that CANNOT hang. The first card run (2026-10-10) showed that everything except two gather streams on one fabric link works with a
# sub-device manager loaded: the mesh opens, the manager loads, eager gathers on both sub-devices (own semaphores, two queues) are exact, the traces capture and replay solo exactly. Those arms, timed in blocks (20 rounds
# after 4 warm-ups): a trace of 24 all-gathers on the target sub-device alone, on the drafter sub-device alone, CHAINED by an event (target on queue 0, record_event, queue 1 waits, drafter: the event's cost with
# collectives in flight). Nothing here puts two gather streams in flight together, so nothing here can deadlock the mesh (the arm once called one_queue, both traces from queue 0, WAS such an arm: both
# gathers ran on link 0, and it hung in the link-offset run of 2026-10-11; it now needs the link-1 graft and lives in the separate-links pack).
# READ: 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=SAFE-PASS' with t_ms, d_ms, chained_ms and bytes=identical; the last stdout line is the JSON (kind subdev-h2), with every byte comparison.
# It judges no overlap: SAFE-PASS says the sub-device collectives are exact and what the serial schedules cost. The overlap itself is H2c (a hang is expected there) and the separate-links arm, which needs the prepared
# link-offset graft (optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/ag_link_offset.patch, not built into any image) and reads NOT-RUN here.
# TIMED: pause the ARC runners. Duration (estimate): 30 min (the box below bounds the probe; the fabric step's own limit is 45).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env): this pack builds nothing, and any C2 image carries the tt-metal sub-device bindings
# it needs (the harnesses mount this checkout's files). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=subdev
C2_FABRIC=FABRIC_1D
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
